{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted","id":1344650,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Archer Advice Wanted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T07:06:54-07:00","id":1344650,"title":"Dragon-Blooded Archer Advice Wanted","content":"I'm trying to build a &quot;combat optimized&quot; (starting character) Dynast who uses archery to destroy her foes.<br /> <br /> My first thought was a Wood Aspect who rode a fearsome beast like a Tyrant Lizard, or Hundred Rivers or a Pestletail, peppering foes with arrows whilst using the mount for speed and close defence. Then I saw that Wood Dragon Form needs a staff or a longbow -- and you can't use a longbow mounted. And the good Survival and Ride Charms seem to be Air aspected... and Air Archery doesn't seem too shabby. (Well Burning Fang Strike needs a Fire Aura.)<br /> <br /> Then I cracked open Arms and thought &quot;Emerald Chevalier is a pretty nice platform for an archer&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is for a combat heavy, monster of the week, &quot;And I'll Form the Head&quot; kind of game (we're adding a third player to Dynasty of Dovak who wants a pregen to drop-in, drop-out of the Ganan sessions -- first foe is an army of hobgoblins).<br /> <br /> Any advice on how to build an effective Deeb archer in 3E, sample builds, need combos, common pitfalls would be gratefully received.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">Master cylinder.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-30-2019, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T07:25:56-07:00","id":1344651,"title":"","content":"Can't provide much advice numbers wise, but one thing I've noticed is that DB archery is packed full of &quot;you must aim for x turns&quot; Charms, and the only reliable way to aim reflexively is the Wood Signature which is Aura, so keep that in mind when picking an Aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T07:49:26-07:00","id":1344658,"title":"","content":"Well, if you\u2019ve got a Tyrant Lizard familiar, you\u2019re probably less an archer and more a Tyrant Lizard commander. <br /> <br /> You probably want Hopping Firecracker Evasion even though it\u2019s not air or wood, getting out to Short range is worth it. At Essence 2 there isn\u2019t even a huge amount of aura stuff that you need early anyway. Also you might want to consider any leftover points to go into athletics, since getting chased down sucks, although much less an issue in a group and even less of one if you\u2019re using ride whenever you\u2019re outdoors.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll try to think of some today and come up with combos tonight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T09:34:20-07:00","id":1344676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344658#post1344658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you\u2019ve got a Tyrant Lizard familiar</div> </div> </div> </div>See in my head I was picturing an archer on the back of a pestletail, knocking back foes who got too close with Smashing Tail Hammer and using Crimson Fang Bite to finish foes off once they've been riddled with arrows. Then I realised that... really didn't work. Or, at least, I couldn't see a way to make it work that wasn't grossly suboptimal <i>and</i> incredibly fiddly mechanically. Especially as pestletails don't give a speed bonus and don't have Legendary Size. Maybe a shieldback lizard?<br /> <br /> Tyrant Lizard is just my go-to three dot familiar. It's hard to go wrong. A flying horse might be better.<br /> <br /> But if you're advising Dodge and Athletics Charms... well they work better with Warstriders than mounts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T09:55:44-07:00","id":1344681,"title":"","content":"As a defensive mount a Siege Lizard is hard to beat, they can just stand there and Heaven Thunder Hammer anyone foolish enough to approach.<br /> <br /> Flying mounts grant an unbeatable advantage, but the advantage is 100% dependent on the ST. Usually a ST won't just let you win 95% of fights just because you have a flying mount, instead you'll start facing a lot more ranged and flying enemies, so there's only so much you get from the perk in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T10:00:43-07:00","id":1344683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344681#post1344681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a defensive mount a Siege Lizard</div> </div> </div> </div>Is useless because you can't ride them.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, yeah, a Siege Lizard would be IDEAL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T10:08:58-07:00","id":1344684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344683#post1344683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is useless because you can't ride them.<br /> <br /> But otherwise, yeah, a Siege Lizard would be IDEAL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? It says their domestication is extremely unlikely, not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T10:12:36-07:00","id":1344688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344684#post1344684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? It says their domestication is extremely unlikely, not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 555:<br /> &quot;Animals which can be used as mounts have a trait called Speed Bonus.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T10:19:18-07:00","id":1344691,"title":"","content":"Page 202, the little table places a Tyrant-lizard as a &quot;Mount&quot; with a Speed bonus of +2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T11:24:39-07:00","id":1344700,"title":"","content":"Ah I didn't know that, that's too bad. Sorcerous Working to mold a saddle system onto it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T12:31:11-07:00","id":1344717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344676#post1344676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you're advising Dodge and Athletics Charms... well they work better with Warstriders than mounts...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, dodge mostly. Athletics has Soaring Leap which also helps disengage, but if you\u2019re in a group you shouldn\u2019t be contesting rushes TOO often.<br /> <br /> If you want to use wood dragon, which is good because it makes you hella versatile, then no mount, but dodge becomes much more important. You also might find yourself just sitting in melee fighting dudes with your powerbow-wrackstaff more often than not, which might not be what you\u2019re going for.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re going pure bow there\u2019s different tactics. Mounts are obviously helpful, flying ones triply so, but they\u2019re also situational. Do you throw a bunch into Ride, possibly neglecting your unmourned movement abilities, and just hope you\u2019re not fighting in too many areas that you can\u2019t bring your mount? <br /> <br /> Something else to consider is when you are aiming. A lot of DB archery charms double in effectiveness when you aim, or require aiming. If you\u2019re aiming every other turn you can spend 10m on your attack and still remain mote positive throughout the fight. So you can use a full excellency, Death from Nowhere and Sky Calming Draw for every withering attack, and a full excellency, Sky Calming Draw, Arrow Thorn Technique and Drawing Lightning Style on everyone decisive and never really rub out. It also means attacks from medium/long range are possible, just with lower accuracy. Which is better than it seems, you lose out on 2 accuracy but you also can\u2019t be disengaged into. For an archer the worst thing ever is for somebody to disengage from the melee ball into you, because then you lose 6 accuracy and are stuck in with a melee focused guy. Also remember that decisive attack accuracy isn\u2019t penalized for being at long range.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re an air aspect especially Stealth also gets opened up as an option. If your group lets you scout up ahead and sneak you can start combat while hidden, at Long range and as an exalt that should be easy, maybe set up Vanishing Wind Body, aim twice, and then finally reveal yourself by shooting. Then just keep aiming and/or shooting as they charge towards you, and pull them right into your waiting allies. <br /> <br /> On the other hand if you\u2019re a mounted wood aspect I recommend Daring Venture and survival as a focus. Don\u2019t bother much with athletics unless you have spare charms and points, it\u2019s only for when you\u2019re being chased down and also unmounted. It\u2019s kind of an edge case at that point. Also with 3 non-charm autosuccesses to tracking from Hundred Rivers, Stalking Wolf Persuit, and Quarry Revelation Technique you\u2019ll be able to track down just about anything anywhere. Even Solars will have trouble shaking that. Also try to find medium barding for your Wolf, you ignore the mobility penalty with your excellency anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T13:23:14-07:00","id":1344736,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, there\u2019s also range dipping if you want to attack each turn. Turn 1 you\u2019re at Short, you attack and retreat to Medium. Turn 2 you\u2019re at medium, you move to short and attack. Repeat. That way you\u2019re only vulnerable to ranged attacks and being disengaged into about half the time. <br /> <br /> A lot of what range you want to sit at, I think, depends on what you\u2019re fighting. Really fast Fair Folk Cataphracts that can easily pop over to you and engage you? That\u2019s probably something you want to fight at medium range, maybe even Long. If you\u2019re facing something with like 9 defence and onslaught penalty negators, that\u2019s probably something you want to risk engaging at Short range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T14:13:14-07:00","id":1344746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344717#post1344717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand if you\u2019re a mounted wood aspect I recommend Daring Venture</div> </div> </div> </div>Daring Venture doesn't have the Mounted tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T14:59:15-07:00","id":1344756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344746#post1344746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daring Venture doesn't have the Mounted tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I forgot the distinction isn't Powerbow and Long Powerbow, it's Short Powerbow and Powerbow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T15:34:52-07:00","id":1344760,"title":"","content":"An Evocation could shrink or enlarge a power bow, and green is one of the jade colors that lends itself to shapeshifting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T16:27:39-07:00","id":1344771,"title":"","content":"Here's maybe a few examples I threw together. They're incomplete characters, just assume they have artifacts and whatever other merits are good in combat. Fast Reflexes and Fleet of Foot or whatever you like.<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Monk<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attributes and Abilities</span><br /> <br /> 3 Strength<br /> 5 Dexterity<br /> 5 Stamina<br /> <br /> 1 Charisma<br /> 1 Manipulation<br /> 5 Appearance<br /> <br /> 5 Perception<br /> 1 Intelligence<br /> 3 Wits<br /> <br /> 5 <b>Archery </b><br /> 3 <b>Athletics </b><br /> 5 <b>Awareness </b><br /> 1 <b>Brawl </b><br /> 5 <b>Dodge </b><br /> 3 Integrity<br /> 5 <b>Wood Dragon </b><br /> 3 <b>Performance</b><br /> 5 <b>Resistance</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> Dodge<br /> Brawl<br /> Archery<br /> Awareness<br /> Athletics<br /> <br /> Wood Dragon (5)<br /> Wood Dragon Vitality<br /> Eyes of the Wood Dragon<br /> Mind-Over-Body Meditation<br /> Soul-Marking Style<br /> Wood Dragon Form<br /> <br /> Archery (6)<br /> Harvest of the Hunter<br /> Sky-Calming Draw<br /> Arrow Thorn Technique<br /> Life Swelling Sap Strike<br /> Death From Nowhere<br /> Spring Follows Winter<br /> <br /> Athletics (1)<br /> Soaring Leap Technique<br /> <br /> Resistance (3)<br /> Ox-Body x3<br /> <br /> Bonus Points Spent<br /> 2 Archery<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 2 Dodge<br /> 2 Wood Dragon<br /> 2 Resistance<br /> 8 Stamina<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> This guy is just really straightforward. Either run in there and start punching with Wood Dragon or hang back and fire arrows, in either aim-shoot-aim mote conservation mode, or flurrying shots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Air Dragon Stealth Archer (yay skyrim meme)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attributes and Abilities</span><br /> <br /> 3 Strength<br /> 5 Dexterity<br /> 3 Stamina<br /> <br /> 1 Charisma<br /> 4 Manipulation<br /> 2 Appearance<br /> <br /> 5 Perception<br /> 1 Intelligence<br /> 5 Wits<br /> <br /> 5 <b>Archery </b><br /> 5 <b>Athletics </b><br /> 5 <b>Awareness </b><br /> 5 <b>Dodge </b><br /> 3 Integrity<br /> 5 <b>Stealth</b><br /> 3 <b>Resistance</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Charms</span><br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> Dodge<br /> Awareness<br /> Archery<br /> Stealth<br /> Athletics<br /> <br /> <br /> Archery (5)<br /> Harvest of the Hunter<br /> Sky-Calming Draw<br /> Arrow Thorn Technique<br /> Death From Nowhere<br /> Drawing Lightning Style<br /> <br /> Stealth (2)<br /> Soundless Action Prana<br /> Vanishing Wind-Body Technique<br /> <br /> Athletics (2)<br /> Soaring Leap Technique<br /> Incense Smoke Ladder<br /> <br /> Awareness (4)<br /> Deep-Listening Palm<br /> All-Encompassing Earth Sense<br /> Cloud Piercing Focus<br /> Feeling the Earth's Bones<br /> <br /> Resistance (2)<br /> Ox-Body Tech x2<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bonus Points Spent</span><br /> 2 Archery<br /> 2 Athletics<br /> 2 Dodge<br /> 2 Stealth<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 8 Perception<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> This guy is kind of a lone-wolf, although still within his circle. Charms like Flowing Shadow Stance and Stalking Wolf Attitude are pretty clear to me that &quot;Join battle and then stalk enemy until finally breaking concealment and attacking.&quot; is 100% intentional game design. So if you can get just into bow-shot range, and set up as many things as you can while the enemy searches for you, and then hopefully break that stealth with a big powerful bowshot, and then harry them with more arrows as they charge you.<br /> <br /> The DB charms to both ignore visual and environmental penalties to archery attacks as well as perception make it way better if you can launch this sneak attack along side environmental factors. Good luck finding a stealth focused exalt at Long range, in the dark, during a rainstorm. If you want you can even grab sorcery to fix up the weather for you. Otherwise a lot of the benefit of those charms is dependent on your ST remembering that weather is a thing, and specifically epic high fantasy weather.<br /> <br /> He's also just good at scouting ahead for information, and his high perception means that he'll notice enemy patrols coming way before they have the chance to spot him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wood Dragon Hunter<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attributes and Abilities</span><br /> <br /> 3 Strength<br /> 5 Dexterity<br /> 3 Stamina<br /> <br /> 3 Charisma<br /> 2 Manipulation<br /> 2 Appearance<br /> <br /> 5 Perception<br /> 1 Intelligence<br /> 3 Wits<br /> <br /> 5 <b>Archery </b><br /> 3 <b>Athletics </b><br /> 5 <b>Awareness </b><br /> 5 <b>Dodge </b><br /> 3 Integrity<br /> 5 <b>Ride</b><br /> 5 <b>Resistance</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Charms</span><br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> Dodge<br /> Awareness<br /> Archery<br /> Ride<br /> Survival<br /> <br /> <br /> Archery (6)<br /> Harvest of the Hunter<br /> Sky-Calming Draw<br /> Arrow Thorn Technique<br /> Live Swelling Sap Strike<br /> Death From Nowhere<br /> Spring Follows Winter<br /> <br /> Ride (3)<br /> Tread Rooted in Life<br /> Heaven Racing Leap<br /> Reins-Like-Roots-Unity<br /> <br /> Survival (4)<br /> Quarry Revelation Technique<br /> Stalking Wolf Pursuit<br /> Beast Taming Aspect<br /> Mother-of-Beasts Mastery<br /> <br /> Resistance (2)<br /> Ox-Body Tech x2<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bonus Points Spent</span><br /> 2 Archery<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 2 Dodge<br /> 2 Ride<br /> 2 Awareness<br /> 8 Perception<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Hunter rides on some kind of great beast, maybe something that flies, although more likely something that can stay close to the ground to track her prey. In combat she uses Ride to retreat to a safe distance and run circles around the enemy, being faster than just about anything else out there. In fact she's so fast that she almost wants somebody to come chasing her. With Tread Rooted in Life, especially once she has the other elemental upgrades, trying to get her into melee is a fool's errand, she can happily gallop through the densest forest or over uneven rocks slick with seawater.<br /> <br /> Again, very ST dependent on remembering about different and difficult terrain and stuff. Either that or try to position yourself to take advantage of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:16:00-07:00","id":1344874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344760#post1344760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Evocation could shrink or enlarge a power bow, and green is one of the jade colors that lends itself to shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've seen in Arms that weapon tags aren't set in stone (there's a Spear with Disarming for starters), and the old version of the Ultimately Useful Tube did something similiar (the current version still has multiple weapon modes).<br /> <br /> The question I have is &quot;how does this look mechanically&quot;?<br /> <br /> Is such a transformation suitable as an Attunement bonus? Does it push the weapon to 4 dots? 5? What sort of Evocations grow from such a weapon? Does the growth happen Reflexively, is it a Simple Charm, or does it grow and shrink over the course of an hour?<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of cool potential with this concept, but that it's also a difficult thing to realise and balance properly. There's a lot of questions that need answering -- starting with &quot;why can't you use a powerbow mounted and does my table care?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're willing to stat out such a powerbow, I'd love to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T03:30:50-07:00","id":1344882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344771#post1344771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's maybe a few examples I threw together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant! Thanks!<br /> <br /> So generally speaking, the idea is Aim then Attack throwing on as many Charms as possible, dipping in and out as circumatances dictate. I'm struggling with the timing but if I got this right...<br /> <br /> 1. Start at Short and Aim<br /> 2. Fire with 10m worth of Charms plus Aiming bonus and Reflexively move to Medium<br /> 3. Aim at Medium<br /> 4. Fire with 10m worth of Charms from Medium and Reflexively move to Short; Repeat from Step 1 as needed<br /> <br /> (Obviously moving that out to Medium and Long if in danger of being overrun, or into Close for the Monk and wanting to hit things with your big stick.)<br /> <br /> I love the Stealth build (I'm going to file that one away to use myself), but I wonder what everyone else is doing after you've Joined Battle but before you take your shot?<br /> <br /> Any Artifact/Evocation recommendations? (That Stealth build is crying out for Midnight Thorn... or maybe a Belt of Shadow Walking. Summer's Thunder looks neat too. I think the Monk has to take Daring Venture.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-31-2019, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:05:05-07:00","id":1344915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344882#post1344882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So generally speaking, the idea is Aim then Attack throwing on as many Charms as possible, dipping in and out as circumatances dictate. I'm struggling with the timing but if I got this right...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry, the aim shot weaving and skirmishing in and out of Short range are mutually exclusive options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344882#post1344882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the Stealth build (I'm going to file that one away to use myself), but I wonder what everyone else is doing after you've Joined Battle but before you take your shot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sitting at Extreme range or Extreme 2. Closer is better but whatever range the enemies won\u2019t get a roll to notice them. Hopefully behind some kind of full cover like deep in the tree line or behind a ruin wall or something. From there they activate scenelong charms and wait. It shouldn\u2019t be too long, the only ones rolling on the first 2-3 turns are the enemy making contested perception stealth checks to spot you.<br /> <br /> Also works well if you\u2019re setting up an ambush and lying in wait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344882#post1344882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any Artifact/Evocation recommendations? (That Stealth build is crying out for Midnight Thorn... or maybe a Belt of Shadow Walking. Summer's Thunder looks neat too. I think the Monk has to take Daring Venture.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Summer Thunder for the horse archer, for sure. I mean just look at it. The stealth archer definitely wants that belt, and maybe Moonlit Huntress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:08:07-07:00","id":1344917,"title":"","content":"Mispost please delete","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":".  I can't read 10-31-2019, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T06:29:24-07:00","id":1344923,"title":"","content":"Mispost Deletion of Shame, Essence 3, Computering 4.<br /> <br /> It is said those wise enough to master this technique also acquire a red colored signature. For all we know, this might just be a legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T07:44:37-07:00","id":1344935,"title":"","content":"Also hearthstones. Twice Striking Lightning Prism is always good, at Essence 2 it raises all (Essence) and (Essence/2 rounded up) charms by 1. Also Glory Sphere, that lets you rage a signature charm off chargen. Imagine that stealth archer with Horizon Spanning Arc, or the Hunter with Dragon Among Horses Exaltation. Gem of the Shield Sister Tree can be useful if you\u2019re in a heavily wooded part of Creation. Jewel of the Shining Heart is just good for DBs in general as it lets you get free specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T12:32:42-07:00","id":1345023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1344874#post1344874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why can't you use a powerbow mounted and does my table care?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can answer that. Well not why does your table care, but the other thing. From a numbers standpoint archery and thrown weapons are strictly better as you increase in weight. You just get bonus damage and overwhelming and lose nothing. The only thing that balances that is tags. That\u2019s why the heavy ranged weapons have bad tags like Slow, and the light ones have good tags like Mounted or Concealable. Not all weapons are going to be perfectly balanced, but at least that helps. <br /> <br /> Powerbows standing 2 meters tall makes them awkward to use on horseback, but I don\u2019t think there\u2019s necessarily a big reason you couldn\u2019t make a composite powerbow. It would be strictly better than a short powerbow but I don\u2019t think it would be broken, although combining cavalry with archery is already extremely powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-31-2019, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:27:54-07:00","id":1345061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1345023#post1345023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can answer that. Well not why does your table care, but the other thing. From a numbers standpoint archery and thrown weapons are strictly better as you increase in weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So?<br /> <br /> Some weapons are strictly better than others.<br /> <br /> Composite bows are Medium Archery weapons with all the tags of a longbow, plus Mounted. (Or all the tags of a short bow, +2 Damage.)<br /> <br /> Longbows can be used with more Martial Arts than shortbows... as well as doing more damage. Then there's the question of if a bow is better than a lance -- if a bow is a suboptimal weapon, is it bad if it's slightly less suboptimal?<br /> <br /> Is a powerbow not having Mounted important in a way that a chopping sword not having Thrown (Short) isn't?<br /> <br /> Exalted has long had the ethos that some weapons are better than others.<br /> <br /> I don't think a composite bow solves the Form weapon problem though.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying your explaination is wrong, but my querry is &quot;what is the implication?&quot; What breaks if you change it? What was the intention here? Why should a long powerbow not be strictly better?<br /> <br /> If we're trying to inventivise short powerbows, it makes more sense to make a short powerbow that can be used as a staff than a long powerbow that can be used Mounted. If we're trying to nerf Mounted combat, neither option is good. If we're trying to incentivise archery on foot, then a shape-shifting powerbow might be just the ticket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-31-2019, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:32:21-07:00","id":1345062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1345023#post1345023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Powerbows standing 2 meters tall makes them awkward to use on horseback, but I don\u2019t think there\u2019s necessarily a big reason you couldn\u2019t make a composite powerbow. It would be strictly better than a short powerbow but I don\u2019t think it would be broken, although combining cavalry with archery is already extremely powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>My theory is that a short powerbow is in the relevant sense already composite. Magical Materials have stretching and compressing strength better than any material, what would you composite them with? Possibly other magical materials, but the differences between them aren't generally expressed in terms of what kind of pressure they are strong against.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, this theory is from the point of view of &quot;I want an explanation of why the book doesn't write up composite powerbow&quot;, not &quot;I want an explanation of how my character has a composite powerbow&quot;<br /> <br /> The other argument is that mortal composite bows are balanced by costing more (Albeit on a fairly vague scale that is easy to mostly surpass), so an artifact composite bow should cost more in some artifacty sense (ie. being mounted and a medium weapon would be the attunement bonus or something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:04:55-07:00","id":1345114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1345061#post1345061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying your explaination is wrong, but my querry is &quot;what is the implication?&quot; What breaks if you change it? What was the intention here? Why should a long powerbow not be strictly better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully there's a fair variety of different weapons that either have their own niche, or are simply not so much worse than other weapons that they feel unusable. As to why Wood Dragon can't use short powerbows, it's probably just a height thing. Artifact staves are at least as tall as your character, powerbow height is the same, shortbows are much shorter. I don't imagine that has anything to do with balance.<br /> <br /> Allowing longbows, or a type of medium archery weapon anyway, to be usable on horseback is probably a little overpowered, but not broken. It's not like the whole balance of the game is going to get shaken for doing that. The best option might be a bow that's got an evocation to make it change from short to long. Like it's got a worn, dark green bow to it, and then after putting a bit of Essence into it, the tips become the bright green of new growth and extend an additional couple of feet to become a longbow.<br /> <br /> I'd say the first evocation, but it awakens for free if resonant, one mote reflexive, can revert to short bow at any time by dropping the mote commitment. I'm not sure where to take it from there. Maybe a charm with Harvest the Hunter as a pre-req that allows you to instantly grow a special arrow out of it right before firing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T12:44:58-08:00","id":1355041,"title":"","content":"The time for this is probably long gone, but I think paradoxically a strong combat character should sacrifice some of their starting power for faster training times- training charms like Elemental Concentration Trance have always been very much appreciated (especially if you have a circle with a solar who can just train everyone up ASAP). Stone of Acrid Understanding has also been very much coveted in games I've played in, although those were all under the same storyteller so I might not have an accurate view of how valuable training time and whatnot is in other peoples games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25854-santova","name":"Santova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:56:34-08:00","id":1355077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Santova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1355041#post1355041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The time for this is probably long gone, but I think paradoxically a strong combat character should sacrifice some of their starting power for faster training times- training charms like Elemental Concentration Trance have always been very much appreciated (especially if you have a circle with a solar who can just train everyone up ASAP). Stone of Acrid Understanding has also been very much coveted in games I've played in, although those were all under the same storyteller so I might not have an accurate view of how valuable training time and whatnot is in other peoples games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well depending on your point of view, you're either not too late or about five years too late.<br /> <br /> Player 3 hasn't actually joined yet. I've drafted an NPC sheet based on the advice in this thread, but we've yet to actually use it. So... any advice is still very welcome.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Draft<br /> <br /> Mnemon Gracious Pealing Melody<br /> Wood Aspect<br /> Pasiap's Stair<br /> The Adopted Archer<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Charisma 5<br /> Manipulation 4<br /> Appearance 2<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 3<br /> <br /> Wood Aspect Abilities (and Specialities) (9 BP)<br /> <br /> Archery 5 (Shortbow)<br /> Medicine 2<br /> Performance 5<br /> Ride 5 (Giant Lizards)<br /> Survival 5<br /> <br /> Favored Abilities (9 BP)<br /> <br /> Athletics 1<br /> Awareness 5<br /> Dodge 5 (Mounted)<br /> Integrity 2<br /> War 3 (Mounted Combat)<br /> <br /> Other Abilities<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Presence 3<br /> Resistance 1 (In the Saddle)<br /> Socialize 3<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Low Realm)<br /> <br /> Artifact 3 (Summer's Thunder, Short Powerbow)<br /> Artifact 4 (Spider Silk Shirt, Light Armor)<br /> Familiar 3 (Clapper, A Shieldback Lizard)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Allies 3 (Mnemon Ferad, Husband)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (Riverspeak)<br /> (Dynastic Freebie) Language (High Realm)<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Archery: Unobstructed Hunter's Aim<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Dodge: Threshold Warding Stance<br /> 4. Integrity: Granite Curtain of Serenity<br /> 5. Ride: Scattered Hoof Falls<br /> <br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Medicine: Master Healer Meditation<br /> 2. Medicine: Wound-Closing Technique<br /> 3. Performance: Talented Improvisation<br /> 4. Performance: Soul-Stirring Performance<br /> 5. Performance: Heart-Strengthening Defense<br /> 6. Performance: Harmonious Life-Affirming Song<br /> 7. Ride: Heaven (G)Racing Leap<br /> 9. Survival: Ration Enhancing Method<br /> 10. Survival: Beast Taming Aspect<br /> 11. Survival: Mother of Beast's Mastery<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> 12. Summer's Thunder: Hooves Like Sunlight<br /> 13. Summer's Thunder: Nook-and-Cranny Unity<br /> 14. Summer's Thunder: Laughing Stallion Escape<br /> 15. Summer's Thunder: Skirmisher's Piercing Deliverance<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> Defining Tie: Clapper (Motherly Love)<br /> Major Tie: Mnemon Ferad (Husband)<br /> Major Tie: Mnemon Jorod (Secret son)<br /> Minor Tie: Slavers (Disgust)<br /> Defining Principle: I am an Upright Soldier<br /> Major Principle: The Immaculate Philosophy<br /> <br /> Combat<br /> Evasion 6+1<br /> Parry 3<br /> <br /> Soak 7 Hardness 4<br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> <br /> Resist Poison: 6(+1) dice<br /> <br /> Summer's Thunder: Accuracy 10/16/14/12/- (11 Decisive)(+6, 6m); Damage 12 (3 OVR; +1, 3m); Archery (Long), Mounted, Lethal<br /> <br /> Rush: 6 (12 Mounted, +3 successes 6m)<br /> Disengage: 10 (12 Mounted, +3 successes 6m)<br /> <br /> Join Battle: 8 dice<br /> <br /> Command Mounted Troops: 8 dice (+4, reroll 6s, 4m)<br /> <br /> Social<br /> Charismatic Performance 10 dice<br /> <br /> Resolve 3 (+1, ignore -1 from wounds, deprivation or poison, 2m)<br /> Guile 3<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (22, 9 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x2<br /> -2 x2<br /> -4 x1<br /> Incap<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On the other hand... this is for a 3E game. I did specify Third Edition in the original post. I really don't need advice on how to build a 2E/2.5 Deeb. I could write the book on how to build a 2E Deeb, so your advice is about five years too late on that front. Elemental Concentration Trance doesn't work like that anymore. (3E is not a perfect game, I complain about it a lot. But it's pretty good, and I would recommend that anyone still trying to make 2E work take a look at the current rules.)<br /> <br /> You do raise an interesting point on training times. We play that if it's plausible that you have been training the trait in question (from the beginning of the game -- you don't get to say your 60 year old has 60 years of training time banked), then you have been training the trait in question. It's not a strictly RAW reading, but it allows you to keep the game moving along without too much downtime. If you've never used the trait in question or sought out a trainer or anything then it's probably not plausible. Or if you've been training half-a-dozen other things in the same period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-15-2019, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T18:07:42-08:00","id":1355097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1355077#post1355077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is for a 3E game. I did specify Third Edition in the original post. I really don't need advice on how to build a 2E/2.5 Deeb. I could write the book on how to build a 2E Deeb, so your advice is about five years too late on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>You absolutely did and I completely spaced on that fact. Furthermore it would probably take me days to build an exalt in 2.5 and even then I'd have no idea how combat prepared they were. I know nothing about 3E so my comments probably aren't very helpful in either situation. That said, I'm sharing them anyways! <br /> High charisma and manipulation rather than perception and wits surprises me, but I only understand what each on does in the context of 2.5. I can guess that the performance charms would benefit from high social skills, but even then I imagine that a warrior would want to be quick to react and able to track their quarry, spot enemies or traps, etc, more than they would want broader social skills- pure speculation, but it seems like either high charisma or high manipulation would be good enough, rather than pumping both? In 2.5 I think it usually would make more sense to bump appearance and either charisma or manipulation if you had to choose one stat to be a two, since that helps on both the offense and the defense. Sorry if a bunch of uninformed thoughts are grating!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25854-santova","name":"Santova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T21:42:02-08:00","id":1355122,"title":"","content":"I guess it is worth mentioning because DBs have a lot of teamwork themes and charms, that there might be charms which are optimal for you if your allies take them. I tried compiling a list, I likely missed one or two though. <b>Bold</b> entries are ones that have bonus effects when they're you're Hearth, <u>underline</u> entries are entries where there's an added bonus just for being a DB, and <i>italics</i> entries are ones where they're helpful, but actually mostly helpful if you have allies to help out.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 