on Suspiration<br /> <br /> Performance<br /> Heart-Strengthening Defense<br /> Harmonious Life Affirming Song<br /> Life Spiring Symphony<br /> Blossom Hides Thorns<br /> Battle Anthem of Ten Thousand Dragons<br /> <br /> Presence<br /> Unbearable Taunt Technique<br /> Moth to the Candle<br /> Virtuous Mountain Shadow<br /> Spirit Cultivating Leadership<br /> <br /> Ride<br /> <i>Ebony Spur Technique</i><br /> Charge of One Hundred Generals<br /> <br /> Sail<br /> Benediction of the Living Ship<br /> Ship Seizing Dragon Talon<br /> <br /> Socialize<br /> Enticing Flame Feint<br /> <br /> Stealth<br /> Zone of Silence Stance<br /> <br /> Survival<br /> <b>Invoking Nature's Forgiveness</b><br /> <b>Vanishing Tracks Technique</b><br /> Roaring Dragon Font<br /> <b>Tireless Caravan Prana</b><br /> <b>Dragon's Nest Shelter</b><br /> <br /> Thrown<br /> Armor Rupturing Fang<br /> Blinding Spark Throw<br /> Elusive Zephyr Strike<br /> Smoke Burst Eruption<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T06:26:57-08:00","id":1355169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Santova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted?p=1355097#post1355097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You absolutely did and I completely spaced on that fact. Furthermore it would probably take me days to build an exalt in 2.5 and even then I'd have no idea how combat prepared they were. I know nothing about 3E so my comments probably aren't very helpful in either situation. That said, I'm sharing them anyways! <br /> High charisma and manipulation rather than perception and wits surprises me, but I only understand what each on does in the context of 2.5. I can guess that the performance charms would benefit from high social skills, but even then I imagine that a warrior would want to be quick to react and able to track their quarry, spot enemies or traps, etc, more than they would want broader social skills- pure speculation, but it seems like either high charisma or high manipulation would be good enough, rather than pumping both? In 2.5 I think it usually would make more sense to bump appearance and either charisma or manipulation if you had to choose one stat to be a two, since that helps on both the offense and the defense. Sorry if a bunch of uninformed thoughts are grating!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there was a bit of mission creep with this one.<br /> <br /> It's for a player who doesn't want to build their own character but who has a different character creation ethic to me. They liked the idea of the various Performance Charms Deebs have that key off combat, and it's a game with a high social focus.<br /> <br /> What I did was make an Archer I was happy with... then gut it to fit the player specification.<br /> <br /> Manipulation helps offense and defence as you rightly point out, but the Charms they want key off Charisma. Social defenses are very important in 3E as the old Perfect Defense of Diaklave-to-face no longer works. Your advice is still solid. (If it were my character, I'd drop Appearance to 1 and bump Charisma to 5 because of Charms. But the &quot;optimal&quot; build is Charisma 1 Manipulation 5 Appearance 5 -- I discuss this at length in the thread &quot;Is it me or is Appearance kinda rubbish&quot;.)<br /> <br /> Wits is probably the second most important combat stat after Dexterity. Perception is kinda &quot;meh&quot; for Dragon-Blooded as you tend to spot hidden foes with Wits+Awareness now. Awareness is absolutely vital, and Perception is essential for offensive sorcery... but an Archer doesn't really need Perception. It's a 3E thing.<br /> <br /> Your points are well thought through and they make me think about what I'm doing. Not grating at all -- I'm very glad of your input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T08:15:46-08:00","id":1355188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1344650-dragon-blooded-archer-advice-wanted#post1344650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I saw that Wood Dragon Form needs a staff or a longbow -- and you can't use a longbow mounted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if anybody mentioned this, but in 3E Wood Dragon Style can't actually be used to make ranged attacks (well, at least not outside of the effects of some specific Charm, anyways). Wood Dragon Stylists can simply switch (at will, at no cost) between using their bow as a staff for close combat or using it as a bow with Archery Charms to make ranged attacks.<br /> <br /> This is in the Style's description in the Dragon-Blooded book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T10:13:37-08:00","id":1355205,"title":"","content":"Right. That's the draw.<br /> <br /> Mounted is +1 Parry. Staff is +1 Parry. Wood Dragon gives effects like healing. Wood Dragon can be practised unarmed. <br /> <br /> Normally, hitting an archer with an undodgable attack is bad news. That archer being able to say &quot;that's ok -- I apply my resting Parry of 8&quot; is what appeals.<br /> <br /> Plus &quot;haha! We disarmed the archer... oh god she's beating us to death with her barehands!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}